## Results — split `test`

140 photos: 90 hard, 30 clean, 20 out-of-catalogue

### Headline

| set | R@1 SKU | R@1 style | R@5 SKU | median rank of truth | median latency |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| clean | 0.067 [0.000, 0.167] | 0.067 [0.000, 0.167] | 0.067 [0.000, 0.167] | 1 | 133 ms |
| hard | 0.022 [0.000, 0.067] | 0.022 [0.000, 0.067] | 0.044 [0.000, 0.111] | 4 | 131 ms |

95% intervals are cluster bootstrap resampling **items**, not photos.

### The gap between the two halves (paired by item, McNemar exact)

- clean-right/hard-wrong: **4**, clean-wrong/hard-right: **0**
- accuracy drop: **+4.4 pp** over 90 pairs, p = 0.125

### Accuracy by failure condition

| condition | n | R@1 SKU | 95% Wilson | R@1 style |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| low_light | 17 | 0.000 | [0.000, 0.184] | 0.000 |
| defocus | 24 | 0.000 | [0.000, 0.138] | 0.000 |
| off_angle | 21 | 0.000 | [0.000, 0.155] | 0.000 |
| partial_occlusion | 8 | 0.000 | [0.000, 0.324] | 0.000 |
| cluttered_background | 29 | 0.034 | [0.006, 0.172] | 0.034 |
| motion_blur | 25 | 0.040 | [0.007, 0.195] | 0.040 |
| small_in_frame | 14 | 0.071 | [0.013, 0.315] | 0.071 |
| specular_reflection | 7 | 0.143 | [0.026, 0.513] | 0.143 |

> Cells are small. At n=10 a 95% interval spans roughly ±25 pp, so the **ordering** of these conditions is not resolvable from this set. The marginal-effects table and the synthetic dose-response sweep are what the condition ranking should be read from.

### Marginal effect of each condition (exploratory)

| condition | n | log-odds | 95% CI | avg marginal effect |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| defocus | 24 | -0.37 | [-0.78, -0.28] | -0.7 pp |
| off_angle | 21 | -0.31 | [-0.67, -0.22] | -0.6 pp |
| low_light | 17 | -0.30 | [-0.72, -0.21] | -0.6 pp |
| partial_occlusion | 8 | -0.13 | [-0.32, -0.06] | -0.3 pp |
| cluttered_background | 29 | +0.21 | [+0.11, +0.62] | +0.5 pp |
| motion_blur | 25 | +0.35 | [+0.23, +0.72] | +0.8 pp |
| small_in_frame | 14 | +0.48 | [+0.37, +0.86] | +1.2 pp |
| specular_reflection | 7 | +0.70 | [+0.60, +1.41] | +2.0 pp |

> Conditions co-occur, so per-condition accuracy above is confounded. This fits correctness on the condition indicator matrix to estimate each condition's marginal contribution. Penalised and bootstrapped by item; **exploratory** at this sample size.

### Dose response

Each additional adverse condition multiplies the odds of a correct match by **1.469**.

| # conditions | n | accuracy | 95% Wilson |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 46 | 0.022 | [0.004, 0.113] |
| 2 | 33 | 0.000 | [0.000, 0.104] |
| 3 | 11 | 0.091 | [0.016, 0.377] |

### Refusal

- AUROC in-catalogue vs out-of-catalogue: **0.502** (120 in, 20 out)

| outcome | count / rate |
|---|---|
| in-catalogue, accepted & correct | 3 |
| in-catalogue, accepted & **wrong** | 25 |
| in-catalogue, refused (FRR) | 92 (0.767) |
| out-of-catalogue, accepted (**FAR**) | 0.300 |
| **wrong-accept rate** | 0.208 |

> The wrong-accept rate is the error a user actually feels, and a bare FAR/FRR pair hides it.

- AURC **0.963**, excess over oracle (E-AURC) **0.064** — E-AURC isolates how well confidence *ranks* its own errors from how many there are.


